          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000029\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"A clear, careful rescue turns into an honest partial loss and propagation of two tips; the damp compost plugs provide a concrete ending, though the prose is somewhat adult and procedural for young children.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000057\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":9,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Mina follows Rosa's specific advice to water and shade the seedlings, producing a logical, secure resolution beneath the greenish screen.\" ,\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000047\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"The lack of permission to use the screen leads sensibly to partial shade and saving cuttings; its ending is concrete and candid about the original tray.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000073\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":9,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Advice about the screen changes Mina's response from watering alone to watering plus shelter, ending with visibly steadier seedlings.\" ,\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000034\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Limited water and unavailable shade make the recovery incomplete, so Mina salvages firm tips; this is coherent and responsibly resolved, if somewhat technical.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000043\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"With no shade cloth, Mina waters, moves the tray, and preserves viable tips; the practical choices lead cleanly to the partial-rescue ending.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000068\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Rosa's explanation that the screen is gone motivates Mina's shaded-shelf solution and eventual propagation, though repeated care details slow the story.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000096\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":9,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Mina receives usable instructions, waters carefully, and installs the screen correctly; the protected tray beneath softened light gives a satisfying concrete outcome.\" ,\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000005\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":9,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"A streamlined version of the successful water-and-screen rescue, with a clear causal turn and a stable final image of seedlings under shade.\" ,\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000085\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"The missing screen and limited water credibly prevent a full rescue, while Mina's rooted cuttings offer a concrete, honest partial success.\" ,\"group_id\":0}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":1,\"causal_path\":2,\"ending\":2,\"language\":2,\"overall\":2},\"diversity_evidence\":\"All ten stories share Mina's attempt to save Rosa's heat-stressed seedlings with Ivo's borrowed watering can. The meaningful branch is narrow: screen-assisted stabilization in s000057, s000073, s000096, and s000005 versus shaded-shelf care followed by salvaging cuttings in s000029, s000047, s000034, s000043, s000068, and s000085. Most wording, objects, actions, and outcomes are repeated, with only minor variants in water supply, permission, and phrasing.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"group_id\":0,\"summary\":\"Mina waters the distressed tray but cannot use a working screen, moves it to partial shade, and saves surviving growth by rooting cuttings after the tray remains too weak.\"},{\"group_id\":1,\"summary\":\"After Rosa authorizes and explains the screen, Mina waters the tray and shades it properly, leaving the seedlings stabilized for the afternoon.\"}]}"
        }
